[64.850214, "o", "#!/bin/bash\r\n# Flush existing rules\r\niptables -F\r\niptables -t nat -F\r\n\r\n# Default policies\r\niptables -P INPUT DROP\r\niptables -P FORWARD DROP\r\niptables -P OUTPUT ACCEPT\r\n\r\n# Allow established connections\r\niptables -A INPUT -m state --state ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT\r\niptables -A FORWARD -m state --state ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT\r\n\r\n# Allow SSH to gateway\r\niptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 22 -j ACCEPT\r\n\r\n# Allow inference subnet to registry on port 5000 (FIXED: moved to FORWARD chain)\r\niptables -A FORWARD -s 10.200.0.0/16 -d 10.100.0.42 -p tcp --dport 5000 -j ACCEPT\r\n\r\n# NAT for outbound\r\niptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 10.200.0.0/16 -o eth2 -j MASQUERADE\r\n\r\n# General forwarding between networks\r\n"]
[64.850305, "o", "iptables -A FORWARD -i eth1 -o eth2 -j ACCEPT\r\niptables -A FORWARD -i eth2 -o eth1 -j ACCEPT\r\n"]
[64.850461, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[64.850502, "o", "root@acd29e238634:/home/user/firewall# "]
[81.363044, "i", "cat > FIXES_APPLIED.txt << 'EOF'\nFIREWALL RULES FIXED - Summary\n================================\n\nPROBLEMS IDENTIFIED:\n\n1. WRONG CHAIN (Line 18 in original):\n   - Rule was in INPUT chain: iptables -A INPUT -s 10.200.0.0/16 -p tcp --dport 5000 -j ACCEPT\n   - INPUT chain only applies to traffic destined FOR the gateway itself\n   - Traffic being forwarded THROUGH the gateway needs FORWARD chain rules\n\n2. EXPLICIT DROP BLOCKING TRAFFIC (Lines 23-24 in original):\n   - iptables -A FORWARD -s 10.200.0.0/16 -d 10.100.0.0/16 -j DROP\n   - This blocked ALL traffic from inference subnet to registry subnet\n   - Came BEFORE the general ACCEPT rule, so matched first and dropped packets\n   - Comment said \"Block known bad actors\" but blocked entire legitimate subnet\n\n3. RULE ORDERING:\n   - DROP rule on line 24 came before ACCEPT rule on line 27\n   - iptables processes rules top-to-bottom, stops at first match\n   - Traffic was dropped before reaching the ACCEPT rule\n\nFIXES APPLIED:\n\n1. Moved port 5000 rule to FORWARD chain (li"]
[81.363173, "i", "ne 19):\n   iptables -A FORWARD -s 10.200.0.0/16 -d 10.100.0.42 -p tcp --dport 5000 -j ACCEPT\n\n2. Removed the problematic DROP rules entirely\n\n3. Added bidirectional forwarding rules for return traffic:\n   iptables -A FORWARD -i eth1 -o eth2 -j ACCEPT\n   iptables -A FORWARD -i eth2 -o eth1 -j ACCEPT\n\n4. Made destination more specific (10.100.0.42 instead of 10.100.0.0/16)\n\nRESULT:\nTraffic from ML inference service (10.200.0.0/16) can now reach model registry (10.100.0.42:5000)\nEOF\n"]
[81.363212, "o", "cat > FIXES_APPLIED.txt << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[81.363246, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[81.363273, "o", "> "]
[81.363345, "o", "FIREWALL RULES FIXED - Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[81.363374, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[81.363405, "o", "> "]
[81.363471, "o", "================================\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[81.363502, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[81.363534, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[81.363595, "o", "PROBLEMS IDENTIFIED:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
